  "name": "ORYVIA",
  "description": "ORYVIA is a proprietary local workstation for genotype-phenotype analysis and candidate review in plant quantitative genetics. It connects input validation, GLM, MLM, native FarmCPU and ORYVIA association models with posterior-effect estimation, independent effect checks, prediction calibration, scientific plots and data-specific causal analyses. These analyses retain their stated inputs and interpretation; causal workflows require an explicit exposure/outcome design and identifying assumptions. The scientific application is supplied separately under authorization. A public MIT-licensed launcher can inspect and register an authorized Unix package, prepare its environment explicitly, and invoke its start, stop and environment checks. The launcher contains no scientific engine or research data. Installing the launcher alone does not install the application.",
